{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ee820b91-48e1-447b-b577-90f117dce7dc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b03b131cb4af0db2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-javj8jya/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Per-project GPU-hour report computation with CSV export and stable API\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the reporting backend for GPU chargeback: computation of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, built on the metering data delivered by the in-flight metering strategy (never re-implementing collection), and exposure of those reports through CSV export and a stable API that finance tooling can retrieve.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Per-project GPU-hour report computation over administrator-selectable time ranges, sourcing the metering data according to the consumption contract established by the metering schema investigation.\n- A stable API serving the report data for finance tooling, plus CSV export of the same report data.\n- Conformance wiring to the metering strategy's schema once it finalizes, with no duplicate collection or re-metering path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given metered GPU usage data, the report computation returns correct per-project GPU-hour totals for selectable time ranges (verified against the metering data for a known period).\n- Reports are exportable as CSV and retrievable through the documented stable API in a form finance tooling can consume.\n- The report computation reads the metering data source exclusively through the agreed consumption contract — no parallel metering or collection path is introduced.\n- When the metering strategy's schema finalizes, the report implementation is verified conformant against the finalized schema (drift resolved, not worked around).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): report computation portion — per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges.\n- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and the stable API are presentation modes of the same report data and API surface produced for HLR-1 — one surface, not a separately schedulable deliverable.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47890,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b40d7958395545f2","agent_id":"abfce0a9feb4636dc","session_id":"9b38e4b5-1cb5-4536-862e-6126a53124be","uuid":"72d644f1-4f54-4ac2-8ac1-4285f3fbbd56","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:03:36.763Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
