{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-876deb3347b74daf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate metering data schema and reporting consumption approach\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate metering data schema and reporting consumption approach\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's open question about the metering data that GPU chargeback reporting consumes: the per-project GPU-hour usage data is delivered by a separate, in-flight metering strategy, and its schema is not final until that strategy lands. This investigation pins down the schema's current state (fields, granularity, time semantics, access path), assesses its stability and timeline, and produces a documented consumption contract plus a build-vs-wait decision that the report implementation builds against.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Inventory the current state of the metering data deliverable from the metering strategy's artifacts and coordination with its team: fields, per-project attribution, what counts as a GPU-hour, time-range semantics, and access path (metrics surface vs stored data).\n34\t- Assess schema stability: which parts are frozen, which are in flux, and the expected finalization timeline relative to this strategy's reporting work.\n35\t- Confirm the exposure model for the report data source given the platform's architecture constraints (the Dashboard consumes via platform APIs and owns no data plane).\n36\t- Decide and document the consumption approach: build against the draft schema behind a versioned contract/adapter, or gate reporting on finalization; record the fallback for schema drift.\n37\t- Publish a findings and consumption-contract document that the report implementation can build against.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- The metering data schema's current fields, per-project granularity, time semantics, and access path are documented, with cited sources (metering strategy artifacts and team input).\n42\t- A consumption contract for reporting is written and reviewed with the metering strategy's team, covering the data-source interface and time-range semantics.\n43\t- A go/no-go decision on building the report implementation against the draft schema is recorded, with the criteria distinguishing the outcomes and a documented fallback if the schema shifts.\n44\t- Schema-drift risk to the reporting implementation is assessed and its mitigation (versioned contract/adapter or deferral) is recorded.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\tResolves the strategy's open question 1 (metering data schema finalization and external timing risk), which gates implementation of HLR-1 and HLR-2. This epic delivers no HLR directly; it unblocks the report computation, export, and administrator-view work.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ad73f8c77462c4","agent_id":"a1b066e547b0cfa33","session_id":"9b38e4b5-1cb5-4536-862e-6126a53124be","uuid":"7a415fc6-9f56-4b08-ab92-611da268a356","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:05:01.239Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-876deb3347b74daf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
